===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|countable|and|uncountable}} The clear blue colour of the sky; also, a pigment or dye of this colour.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1815|author=w:William Wordsworth|title=s:Extracts from An Evening Walk
|passage=In robes of '''azure'''.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2014|author=w:William H. Gass|title=On Being Blue: A Philosophical Inquiry| page=59| passage=For our blues we have the '''azures''' and ceruleans, lapis lazulis, the light and dusty, the powder blues, the deeps: royal, sapphire, navy, and marine {{...}}}}
#: {{color panel|azure|007FFF}}
# {{lb|en|tincture}} A [[blue]] colour on a [[coat of arms]], represented in engraving by horizontal parallel lines.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1904|author=Arthur Charles Fox-Davies|title=The Art of Heraldry: An Encyclopaedia of Armory|publisher=London : T.C.; & E.C. Jack|page=41
|text=Berington of Chester (on the authority of Harleian manuscript No. 1535) is said to bear a plain shield of azure. Personally I doubt this coat of arms {{nb...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1997|author=Brault|title=Early Blazon|passage=In ''Bb'' [Glover's Roll], the conventional letter ''B'' is used to indicate '''azure''' in most items.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2010|author=E. Baumgaertner Wm E. Baumgaertner|author2=Wm E. Baumgaertner|title=Squires, Knights, Barons, Kings: War and Politics in Fifteenth Century England|publisher=Trafford Publishing|isbn=9781426907692
|text=Sir Henry "Hotspur" Percy: before 1399: or, a lion rampant '''azure''', differentiated with a label gules (a blue lion rampant on a field of gold, differentiated with a red label signifying the first-born son) {{...}} }}
#: {{color panel|azure (heraldry)|0028E9}}
# {{lb|en|poetic}} The unclouded sky; the blue vault above.
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Lost|book=I|passage=Not like those steps / On heaven's '''azure'''.|year=1873}}
#* {{RQ:Blind Ascent of Man|poem=Reapers|page=140|passage=Not a single cloud mars the flawless '''azure'''; / Not a shadow moves o'er the moveless crops; [...]}}
# Any of various widely distributed [[lycaenid]] butterflies of the [[genus]] {{taxfmt|Celastrina|genus}}.
# Any of various Australasian [[lycaenid]] butterflies of the genus {{taxlink|Ogyris|genus}}.
# [[lapis lazuli|Lapis lazuli]].

